           TestSuite "cobol-check expectations"

      * These show the forms an EXPECT can take. They test the fields of
      * EXPECTATIONS.CBL rather than anything in HIKER,
      * so they keep passing while you rewrite HIKER around them.
      * cobol-check counts each EXPECT as one test case.

           TestCase "numeric"
           MOVE 42 TO WS-NUMBER
           EXPECT WS-NUMBER TO BE 42
           EXPECT WS-NUMBER TO EQUAL 42
           EXPECT WS-NUMBER = 42
           EXPECT WS-NUMBER NOT TO BE 54
           EXPECT WS-NUMBER != 54
           EXPECT WS-NUMBER > 41
           EXPECT WS-NUMBER >= 42
           EXPECT WS-NUMBER < 43
           EXPECT WS-NUMBER <= 42

           TestCase "alphanumeric"
           MOVE "Hello, World!" TO WS-TEXT
           EXPECT WS-TEXT TO BE "Hello, World!"
           EXPECT WS-TEXT(8:5) TO BE "World"
           EXPECT WS-TEXT NOT TO BE "Goodbye"

           TestCase "condition names"
           SET WS-SWITCH-IS-ON TO TRUE
           EXPECT WS-SWITCH-IS-ON TO BE TRUE
           MOVE "N" TO WS-SWITCH
           EXPECT WS-SWITCH-IS-ON TO BE FALSE
